WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:16.092
"You destroy Magica!"

2
00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:17.372
Perda cried to Morb.

3
00:00:17.992 --> 00:00:18.932
She turned to Wyssa.

4
00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.793
"You have to stop him!"

5
00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:22.453
Wyssa said nothing.

6
00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:24.874
She was staring at the contraption in horror.

7
00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:27.375
"It's too late," Morb sneered.

8
00:00:27.395 --> 00:00:29.875
"No one can stop me now!"

9
00:00:30.815 --> 00:00:32.376
Zann stared at his parents.

10
00:00:33.056 --> 00:00:36.138
Their bodies twitched as the memory mice scampered over them.

11
00:00:36.158 --> 00:00:40.300
"Are the mice really sucking out my parents' memories?"

12
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.001
he asked.

13
00:00:41.021 --> 00:00:43.862
"That's right, boy," Morb said.

14
00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:45.223
"But don't worry.

15
00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:49.506
Once their memories are emptied, I'll have no further use for your parents.

16
00:00:49.866 --> 00:00:51.887
You can have them back."

17
00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:52.688
Zann shuddered.

18
00:00:52.988 --> 00:00:57.430
He'd never imagined there could be anything worse than being separated from his parents.

19
00:00:58.171 --> 00:00:59.792
Now he wasn't so sure.

20
00:01:00.972 --> 00:01:05.354
He couldn't stand the thought of finding them just in time to watch them forget everything.

21
00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:08.335
Would they remember their old home in First City?

22
00:01:09.056 --> 00:01:11.857
Or that family vacation they'd all taken to the Flower Forest?

23
00:01:12.297 --> 00:01:13.618
Would they even remember him?

24
00:01:14.418 --> 00:01:16.059
Morb turned to the Roodian queen.

25
00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:19.120
"I'm glad you're here to witness this," he taunted.

26
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.501
"Without you, it never could have happened."

27
00:01:23.802 --> 00:01:27.083
Still thinking about the past, Zann stared at his parents.

28
00:01:27.784 --> 00:01:32.167
Then he noticed a couple of memory mice sniffing curiously in his direction.

29
00:01:32.827 --> 00:01:33.848
He looked over at Wyssa.

30
00:01:34.188 --> 00:01:37.010
"How do people invite the mice to eat their memories?"

31
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:37.770
he whispered.

32
00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.772
She appeared confused.

33
00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:43.234
"Simply by opening their minds to them."

34
00:01:43.254 --> 00:01:46.516
"Good." Zann glanced at his friends and Venna.

35
00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:49.738
"Start thinking about Magica," he whispered.

36
00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:52.620
"Any memories you can come up with.

37
00:01:52.941 --> 00:01:54.602
And invite the mice to come to you."

38
00:01:54.622 --> 00:01:57.023
"What?" Perda looked alarmed.

39
00:01:57.043 --> 00:02:00.925
"You mean ask those things to eat our memories?"

40
00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:02.566
Zann nodded.

41
00:02:02.586 --> 00:02:06.287
"There are five of us, and only two of my parents," he said.

42
00:02:07.308 --> 00:02:08.929
"Maybe we can draw the mice away!"

43
00:02:10.169 --> 00:02:11.210
Morb glanced over.

44
00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.050
"What are you whispering about over there?"

45
00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:13.731
he snapped.

46
00:02:14.391 --> 00:02:16.932
"You should be grateful that you're here to see this.

47
00:02:17.852 --> 00:02:20.654
Otherwise you'd have only moments to live."

48
00:02:21.034 --> 00:02:21.594
He smirked.

49
00:02:21.614 --> 00:02:26.156
"Of course, I can't guarantee you have much longer than that.

50
00:02:26.964 --> 00:02:30.126
The Beast of the Otherworld is always hungry."

51
00:02:31.126 --> 00:02:34.028
Zann ignored Morb and focused his thoughts on home.

52
00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:41.092
As more and more memories flooded his mind, Zann tried to send them toward the mice, inviting them

53
00:02:41.112 --> 00:02:41.572
to share.

54
00:02:42.472 --> 00:02:43.793
One mouse wiggled its nose.

55
00:02:44.173 --> 00:02:48.235
Then it jumped down from Zann's father and took a step toward Zann.

56
00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:51.197
A second mouse followed, and then a third.

57
00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:56.500
Soon all the mice were scampering across the room, headed for Zann and his friends.

58
00:02:59.308 --> 00:02:59.588
"N-now what?"

59
00:02:59.748 --> 00:03:04.752
Gliss asked nervously, backing away as far as the troll restraining her would let her.

60
00:03:05.492 --> 00:03:08.915
Once again Morb had turned away to taunt the Roodian queen.

61
00:03:09.715 --> 00:03:14.399
When he finally noticed the memory mice moving away from his machine, he let out a howl of

62
00:03:14.559 --> 00:03:18.121
fury. "To me!"

63
00:03:18.502 --> 00:03:20.143
Wyssa intoned at the same time.

64
00:03:21.364 --> 00:03:26.688
Zann held his breath as Wyssa's spell grabbed his parents and dragged them over to join the others.

65
00:03:28.756 --> 00:03:34.618
A split second later, the trolls were flung against the walls, and a Shield spell appeared around the

66
00:03:34.658 --> 00:03:35.278
rest of the group.

67
00:03:36.118 --> 00:03:39.359
"No!" Morb flung a bolt of energy at Wyssa.

68
00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:43.540
But it bounced off the glowing shield and ricocheted around the room.

69
00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.141
Zann hardly noticed.

70
00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.361
His parents looked dazed and weak.

71
00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:53.403
They stared at him blankly, and for a moment he was afraid it was too late.

72
00:03:54.123 --> 00:03:56.083
Then his mother's eyes brightened.

73
00:03:56.103 --> 00:04:00.253
"Zann?" she whispered, reaching out to touch his face.

74
00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.375
"Is it really you?"

75
00:04:03.416 --> 00:04:05.197
Zann's father smiled feebly.

76
00:04:05.618 --> 00:04:07.820
"We've missed you so much, son."

77
00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.182
"They remember you!"

78
00:04:10.422 --> 00:04:11.203
Perda exclaimed.

79
00:04:12.384 --> 00:04:14.806
"Of course we do," Zann's mother said.

80
00:04:14.826 --> 00:04:18.889
"But my head feels so fuzzy "You're lucky.

81
00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:24.013
The mice probably didn't focus on any particular memory," Wyssa told Zann's parents.

82
00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.776
"They just nibbled away here and there.

83
00:04:27.156 --> 00:04:31.538
You two will be weak for a while, but your memories should come back."

84
00:04:32.378 --> 00:04:34.399
Zann finally looked out through the shield.

85
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:40.902
Morb was gnashing his teeth and stalking back and forth, occasionally blasting a troll.

86
00:04:40.922 --> 00:04:42.603
"It's not enough!"

87
00:04:42.823 --> 00:04:43.243
he cried.

88
00:04:43.263 --> 00:04:45.605
"I still don't have enough power!"

89
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:47.005
"He's right.

90
00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:49.346
Look!" Perda pointed to the tube.

91
00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:53.028
The glowing energy stopped just short of the top.

92
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.183
Morb snarled and then climbed into the machine!

93
00:04:57.203 --> 00:05:00.546
"Even a Void has memories," he hissed.

94
00:05:01.587 --> 00:05:04.650
"I suppose mine will work just as well as any.

95
00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:08.253
I have a few childhood memories I wouldn't mind getting rid of!"

96
00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:11.817
Venna gasped.

97
00:05:11.837 --> 00:05:13.418
"We have to do something!"

98
00:05:14.319 --> 00:05:16.561
"Stand back," Wyssa said grimly.

99
00:05:17.402 --> 00:05:19.824
She waved a hand, and the shield disappeared.

100
00:05:20.532 --> 00:05:24.014
Wyssa sent a huge Blast spell flying toward the contraption.

101
00:05:24.795 --> 00:05:26.596
But it stopped short, fizzling away.

102
00:05:26.616 --> 00:05:28.938
"It's not working!"

103
00:05:29.138 --> 00:05:29.698
Gliss cried.

104
00:05:29.718 --> 00:05:32.660
"I can see that, girl," Wyssa snapped.

105
00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.063
"The power of the Horns is blocking all magic."

106
00:05:36.083 --> 00:05:38.504
"Maybe I can still get through."

107
00:05:39.245 --> 00:05:42.587
Darb handed the mibbit to Gliss and then rushed toward the machine.

108
00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.789
But some unseen force bounced him back.

109
00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.531
He landed on the stone floor with a grunt.

110
00:05:49.311 --> 00:05:49.972
Venna paled.

111
00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:52.405
"There's no way to stop him!

112
00:05:53.205 --> 00:05:54.645
Magica is doomed!"

113
00:05:55.886 --> 00:05:58.466
Morb cackled as the mice continued to feed.

114
00:05:58.986 --> 00:06:02.727
His body slumped weakly, but his eyes glittered with triumph.

115
00:06:03.588 --> 00:06:04.668
"How do you like that?"

116
00:06:04.928 --> 00:06:05.428
he spat.

117
00:06:05.448 --> 00:06:10.910
"It took a Void to figure out how to focus enough magic energy to destroy Magica."

118
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.610
He grinned nastily.

119
00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:19.372
"Then again, who else but a Void could really appreciate the true power of magic energy?

120
00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:21.701
Others take it for granted.

121
00:06:22.342 --> 00:06:28.647
But I could see how something that's harmless when used for small spells can be devastating when used

122
00:06:28.707 --> 00:06:29.888
for large ones!"

123
00:06:29.908 --> 00:06:32.790
"What are we going to do?"

124
00:06:33.011 --> 00:06:33.611
Perda cried.

125
00:06:34.392 --> 00:06:35.373
Zann didn't answer.

126
00:06:35.733 --> 00:06:38.976
All he could do was watch as the tube filled to the top.

127
00:06:39.776 --> 00:06:42.779
Morb brushed the mice off himself and got out of the machine.

128
00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:48.203
His mouth curled into an evil smile as he flung the hatch open.
